SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Network Adequacy Guidance for Plan Year 2026
DESCRIPTION:STATE OF MAINE  \nDEPA RTMENT O F P R OFES SIO NAL  & FINA NCI
 AL  RE GUL ATIO N  \nBUREAU OF  INSU RAN CE  \n \nOffice Location: 76 Nort
 hern Avenue\, Gardiner\, Maine 04345 \nMailing Address: 34 State House Sta
 tion\, Augusta\, Maine 04333 \nwww.maine.gov/pfr/insurance \nPhone: (207) 
 624-8475 TTY: Please Call Maine Relay 711 Consumer Assistance: (800) 300-5
 000 Fax: (207) 624-8599 \nJanet T. Mills \nGovernor \nRobert L. Carey \nSu
 perintendent \nJoan F. Cohen \nCommissioner \nBulletin 487 \nNetwork Adequ
 acy Guidance for Plan Year 2026 \nThe Legislature has approved amendments 
 to Bureau of Insurance Rule Chapter 850 that require \nthe Bureau to estab
 lish new network adequacy standards effective for plan years beginning on 
 or \nafter January 1\, 2026\, and to publish those standards and an except
 ion process in an annual Bureau \nof Insurance bulletin.1  The standards m
 ust equal or exceed the minimum requirements set by the \nCenters for Medi
 care and Medicaid Services (CMS) for qualified health plans  offered on th
 e \nMarketplace.2 \nFor plan years beginning on or after January 1\, 2026\
 , the Superintendent hereby adopts the \nstandards that CMS has adopted fo
 r Medicare Advantage plans in the State of Maine\, as shown in \nthe sprea
 dsheet that is attached as Appendix 1 \, which sets forth maximum distance
  and driving \ntime for primary care and for designated specialty and faci
 lity types\, based on the enrollee’s county \nof residence.  Insurers mu
 st contract with a sufficient number of providers and facilities to ensure
  \nthat at least 90 percent of enrollees in each county can access care wi
 thin the specified travel time \nand distance standards.  Distance and est
 imated driving time  must be measured according to a \nmethodology CMS ref
 ers to as “ geographic distance \,”3 which uses an algorithm designed 
 to \nidentify the most likely driving route\, considering various topograp
 hic factors that consumers \nexperience when traveling to access care. \nI
 nsurers must also continue to meet Rule 850’s requirement to main\nhttps
 ://www.maine.gov/pfr/insurance/sites/maine.gov.pfr.insurance/files/inline-
 files/487.pdf
URL:https://www.maine.gov/pfr/insurance/sites/maine.gov.pfr.insurance/file
 s/inline-files/487.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
